# Cloudflare Pages _redirects

# NOTE: Pages _redirects cannot match on host names, so the old rules for
# linkar52.pages.dev and www.pknslinkar52.com.my never worked here. Those
# redirects (www / pages.dev -> pknslinkar52.com.my, 301) are handled in
# functions/_middleware.js instead.

# EN route only — root serves index.html automatically
# NOTE: rewrite target must be extensionless. Cloudflare Pages auto-redirects
# .html paths to their clean-URL form even as a 200 rewrite target, which was
# turning this into a visible redirect (/en/ -> /index-en) instead of a silent
# rewrite — that's why Google was refusing to index /en/ and picking /index-en
# as the canonical instead.
/en/    /index-en    200
/en     /index-en    200
